\date{2025-12-14T23:55:32Z}
\tag{discrete}
\taxon{Example}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{Some example [propositions](002P):}

\ul{
  \li{\em{Washington, D.C. is the capital city of the United States.}}
  \li{\em{9 is evenly divisible by 3.}}
  \li{\em{Toronto is the capital of Canada.}}
  \li{\em{#{9 < 3}}.}
  \li{\em{Every even natural number greater than 2 can be written
  as the sum of two prime numbers.}}
}

\p{The first two propositions are true.  The next two are false.  The
last one is a famous proposition called the Goldbach Conjecture; we do
not know if it is true or false.  However, all of these are valid
propositions.}
